plugin-hostd-protocol (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Floors only, no ceilings, declared once in packaging/deps.txt; the spec
    and debian/control are generated from it and the floors check refuses
    drift (#64): omx-dsp-devel >= 0.32.4 (0.5.9 declared 0.32.1),
    omx-contract 3.18.0 and plugin-db 0.4.4 as before.
  * python3-plugin-hostd-client, a new noarch package: the protocol's Python
    client ships from here (#47, #45).
  * python3-plugin-hostd-protocol, the Python codec, ships from here with
    epoch 1, above the package plugin-hostd built before (#48, #46).
  * The grammar's quoted-escaped form, a quoted value that is text, for the
    property verbs (#39, omx-clap-core#15).
  * The panel file declares its keys, meters among them (#51).
  * The typed replies have a JSON Schema each, installed under shapesdir,
    and the TypeScript render is published as an npm package (#82, #81); the
    TypeScript client of the protocol, its transport, the generated
    vocabulary and curvePoints, ships in the same package (#87).
  * An untagged empty line, and a whitespace-only one, gets no reply and
    changes no state; a tagged one keeps its answer (#79, #83).
  * phd_note_valid reads no word past count, phd_pin_path_decode writes
    nothing into a size of 0 (#74), and phd_number_in reads one spelling per
    number, in the caller's lo and hi only (#75).
  * The command and feedback markers of mod-host.h that the generator reads
    are back (#80).
  * The installed C headers document their public API with Doxygen (#69,
    #76).
  * The curve families of omx-dsp 0.32.4: the delay and reverb curve
    families and the 37 roles curve_bind takes, with time_response, which a
    curve verb draws as omx-dsp does (#93). The omx-dsp floor is 0.32.4: the
    curve verbs use what omx_curve.h declares from there.
  * rpc_timeout_ms: a silent worker gets SIGTERM first, so it closes its
    JACK client, and SIGKILL only if it has not left two seconds later
    (#89).
  * No epoch on any package of this source (#95).

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:08:07 +0100


plugin-hostd-protocol (0.5.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Built against plugin-db >= 0.4.4 and below 0.5 and omx-dsp >= 0.32.1 and
    below 0.33, the 3.18.0 pass's newest of each, with their ceilings (D30).
  * CI renders against what the channel serves every day, the render check
    alone, and names the served contract packages when it fails (#27, #32).
  * The fuzz seed corpus is held to its generator on every pull request, and
    the generator writes the same corpus in every locale (LC_ALL=C); the
    corpus and both golden transcripts are written again over it (#33, #34).
  * The default CLAP search path holds the folders distributions install
    plugins in, /usr/local/lib/clap, /usr/lib64/clap and /usr/local/lib64/clap,
    after clap/entry.h's: a fresh plugin-hostd learns a first-use pin there
    (plugin-hostd#82, #36).

